        "question_fTH78x": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "WHAT IS COLOSTRUM?",
            "answer": "<p>Colostrum is a form of milk produced by mammals in late pregnancy and the few days after giving birth. It has very high concentrations of vitamins, minerals, protein, fats, immune and growth factors. Ingesting colostrum establishes beneficial bacteria in the digestive tract. </p>"
          }
        },
        "question_Bxtnhn": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "WHAT ARE PROLINE-RICH POLYPEPTIDES (PRP'S)?",
            "answer": "<p>PRPs actively regulate the thymus gland, the bodies central command for the immune system. They can stimulate an underactive immune system, as seen in microbial infections, and/ or they can calm down an overactive immune system as seen in allergies, chemical sensitivities, and autoimmune disease. </p>"
          }
        },
        "question_VrfRd3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "WHAT DOES \"UNDENATURED\" MEAN?",
            "answer": "<p>In the case of whey, in the processing and purification, too much heat for too much time \"cooks\" some the bioactive peptides to deactivate them. When this happens much of the<br/>antioxidant, detoxification and immune support undenatured whey supplies are lost.</p>"
          }
        },
